  "description": "Two weeks. Build something useful. Ship it to BOSS Console. BOSS Contributor Hackathon is an open-source contribution sprint for developers who want to build, fix, improve, and ship meaningful work to BossConsole, an Apache-2.0, multi-platform harness for AI agents. What to Build Pick a useful issue, improvement, integration, UI fix, agent workflow, developer-experience upgrade, or documentation contribution that makes BossConsole better for real users. Prize Pool: 1st place: $500. 2nd place: $300. 3rd place: $200. What We Will Judge Quality. Usefulness. Relevance. Originality. Ownership of your contribution. AI-assisted development is allowed, but the contribution should still show clear thinking and real effort. What Will Not Count Spam PRs. Duplicated submissions. Low-effort changes. Irrelevant contributions. Copied work will not be rewarded. Eligibility Open to students, freshers, professionals, and open-source contributors. Participants should have a GitHub profile and be able to submit a meaningful contribution to the repository.",
